// ═══ the beat ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// She is drawn once. From here on nothing is redrawn — things MOVE.
//
// `pivot` turns everything a turtle has drawn about a point: one angle per
// step, which is one frame, so the flippers sweep instead of being sketched
// again. The angle is a sine, so the stroke slows at the top and the bottom of
// its arc, and the two sides mirror each other about their own shoulders.
//
// `shift` carries the whole animal forward — most of the ground gained on the
// down stroke, the way it works — and gives the near water a breath of its own,
// a pixel or two, out of phase with her.
//
// Five beats of sixty steps. Every step that moves something repaints the
// artwork, which is what a move costs (adr 0012).

